    "description": "<p><i>Reference Book:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Star_Wars_Saga_Edition_Starships_of_the_Galaxy\" title=\"Star Wars Saga Edition Starships of the Galaxy\">Star Wars Saga Edition Starships of the Galaxy</a></i></p><table class=\"wikitable\">\n <tbody>\n  <tr>\n   <th>PASSENGER CONVERSION</th>\n   <th>EMPLACEMENT POINTS</th>\n   <th>AVAILABILITY</th>\n   <th>SIZE RESTRICTION</th>\n   <th>COST</th>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td>Seating</td>\n   <td>1</td>\n   <td>Common</td>\n   <td>-</td>\n   <td>200 (Base)</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td>Quarters</td>\n   <td>10</td>\n   <td>Common</td>\n   <td>Colossal or Larger</td>\n   <td>500 (Base)</td>\n  </tr>\n </tbody>\n</table><p>Some Space Transports and small Capital Ships specialize in transporting passengers instead of cargo. One Passenger Conversion has sufficient room for a number of passengers equal to the ship's <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Cost_Modifier_(Vehicles)\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Cost Modifier (Vehicles)\">Cost Modifier</a>, and these passengers can either have Seating (typically for voyages of only 1 day or less) or Quarters. In either case, these are steerage-quality accommodations (shared rooms, bunk beds, storage lockers, and so on); for higher quality, the ship may also have a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Luxury_Upgrade\" title=\"Luxury Upgrade\">Luxury Upgrade</a>.</p>",
